# Integer16 literal below the minimum

Verifies a negated int16 literal whose signed magnitude is below the 16-bit
minimum is rejected with a compile-time diagnostic through the complete CLI
pipeline.

>>> source
const too_small: int16 = -32769
print(too_small)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: invalid literal `-32769` for type `int16`: number too small to fit in target type at Span { start: 25, end: 31 }

<<< exit
1
